          "number": 5,
          "letter": "E",
          "english": "Today, in so far as researchers can hypothesise, MRS is most easily understood as a slow renewal of finite mental and physical resources. When an employee sits through an ineffective meeting their brain power is essentially being drained away. Meetings drain vitality if they last too long, fail to engage employees or turn into one-sided lectures. The conservation of resources theory, originally proposed in 1989 by Dr Stevan Hobfoll, states that psychological stress occurs when a person's resources are threatened or lost. When resources are low, a person will shift into defence to conserve their remaining supply. In the case of office meetings, where some of employees' most valuable resources are their focus, alertness and motivation, this can mean an abrupt halt in productivity as they take time to recover.",
          "chinese": "如今，就研究人员能够提出的假说而言，会议恢复综合征最容易被理解为有限的脑力和体力资源缓慢恢复的过程。当员工坐着参加一场低效会议时，他们的脑力实际上正在被消耗。如果会议持续时间过长、无法调动员工参与，或演变成单方面的讲座，就会耗损他们的活力。斯特凡·霍布福尔博士于1989年最初提出的资源保存理论认为，当一个人的资源受到威胁或损失时，就会产生心理压力。当资源不足时，人会进入防御状态，以保存剩余的资源。在办公室会议中，员工最宝贵的资源包括专注力、警觉性和积极性，这种情况可能意味着生产力会突然停止，因为他们需要花时间恢复。",
